    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n16602" root="رمح" body-key="r">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رَمُوحٌ</span></b>  and ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رَمَّاحٌ</span></b>  [A horse, or the like, <i>that has
a habit of kicking</i>]. You say <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">دَابَّةٌ رَمُوحٌ عَضُوضٌ</span>
and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عَضَّاضَةٌ</span> ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رَمَّاحَةٌ</span></b> , [<i>A kicking, biting, beast</i>].
(A.) And <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">نَاقَةٌ رَمُوحٌ</span> (tropical:)  <i>A kicking she-camel.</i>
(TA.)

